# confgr-studio is CRLF throughout and tooling that string-matches source
# depends on it. Keep this repo consistent with that.
* text=auto eol=crlf
*.glb binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.stp binary
*.step binary

# EXCEPTION, and it costs 27 tests if it is missing.
#
# vitest transforms a module by hoisting its imports to the very top of the
# file. tools/inspect-model.mjs and tools/declare.mjs both open with a
# `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang, which hoisting pushes to line 3 - where it is
# not a shebang any more, it is a syntax error. Under LF vitest strips it first
# and all is well; under CRLF it does not, and the whole of tests/inspect and
# tests/declare fail with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" and no
# location to work from.
#
# Found the hard way: a `git checkout` of those two files re-wrote them CRLF
# mid-session and 27 tests went red with nothing in the diff to explain it. On a
# machine that had never seen them any other way it would have been the first
# thing a fresh clone did.
#
# Narrow on purpose. The repo stays CRLF as decided above; only the modules
# vitest actually transforms are pinned to LF. Both files are mode 100644, so
# the shebangs are decorative and could have been deleted instead - keeping
# them, and keeping the rule, means the next tool that opens with one is safe
# too.
*.mjs text eol=lf
